===Etymology 2===
[[File:Uranus' Satellite 1986 U10 Discovery Image (cropped).jpg|thumb|The [[planet]] [[Uranus]] photographed on 23 January 1986 by the US [[w:NASA|National Aeronautics and Space Administration]]’s [[space probe]] {{w|Voyager 2}}. The word ''Uranian'' means an [[inhabitant]] of the planet, as well as “of or pertaining to the planet”.]]

From {{suffix|en|Uranus|ian}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=''n.{{sup|1}}'' and ''adj.{{sup|2}}''|noformat=yes|id=220340|date=March 2012|nodot=yes}}; {{R:Lexico|alt=Uranian{{sup|2}}|pos=adj.'' and ''n}}</ref>

